From e10a7ff8f8f5d69c565968e4d4ba934e3b1d4967 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 14:30:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(usernames,rating): collectible NFT usernames and
 composite account rating

Adds two protocol-native subsystems plus their admin surfaces.

Collectible usernames (Fragment-style):
- peer_usernames becomes a multi-username registry: one editable slot per peer
  (old invariant preserved by a partial unique index) plus collectible rows.
  Global name uniqueness keeps a single source of truth, so resolution and
  occupancy checks are unchanged for existing names.
- collectible_usernames holds the asset and its fragment.collectibleInfo
  payload; collectible_username_transfers is an append-only provenance log with
  command-key idempotency.
- fragment.getCollectibleInfo is implemented; the TL usernames vector is now
  built from the registry, and account/channels/bots toggleUsername +
  reorderUsernames stop being no-ops.
- Every projection degrades to the previous single-username behaviour when the
  registry service is absent or errors, so no existing client path can regress.

Composite account rating:
- account_rating is a derived read model (stars, activity, moderation penalty
  and manual adjustment components kept separately) projected into
  userFull.stars_rating and stars_my_pending_rating; pending is self-only.
- Levels use quadratic thresholds; a score that drops applies at once while a
  score that grows parks as pending, which is what the TL field expresses.
- account_rating_events is the contribution ledger; only manual adjustments
  survive a recompute. A background worker recomputes stale rows.

Admin panel: two new tabs (collectible usernames, account ratings) with
listings, detail views with provenance/component breakdown, and mint /
transfer / revoke / burn / recompute / adjust actions routed through the
existing dry-run + command-journal machinery.

Also fixes ensureOfficialSystemUser, which upserted peer_usernames on the
unique index that migration 0149 replaces.
